 "note": "The home check uses /?index=1 rather than a bare / because `url: \"/\"` cannot become a contract step; app.py ignores unrecognised query parameters and serves the home document, so the alias is the same page. Subscriber checks (session: true) reach clone-local inference surfaces: IPVanish gates account creation behind a purchase, so no subscriber state was ever observed on the source. Credentials are deterministic synthetic seed fixtures on @example.invalid. The anonymous auth-boundary redirect is asserted in clone/tests/test_auth.py rather than here, because a gate runner that shares one client across checks is signed in by the time it would run. Each check carries at most one expect_contains value and at most one expect_not_contains value, because a contract step holds at most two assertions and a second value of the same kind would be dropped rather than asserted. Every POST check targets a route that also answers GET and whose form action is declared by exactly one template under clone/frontend/fragments/, so a submit step resolves a real form instead of a guessed selector.",
